            <ArticleTitle>Cholesterol and DNA content in arterial tissue in severe obesity: their relation to some risk factors for ischaemic heart disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>591-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Arterial tissue was obtained from twelve severely obese patients during jejuno-ileal by-pass surgery. The arterial DNA content was inversely correlated with the sum of venous glucose values during an oral glucose tolerance test (rs = -0.72). This observation may have implications on the known relationship between decreased glucose tolerance and early manifestations of atherosclerosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
